  "method": [
    "Stopped fixture mounted read-only. Each trial copies TDB into its own container /tmp and uses a fresh JVM. No product service or dataset was changed.",
    "Native trials assert 100000 Works and 10000 MatchUnits. The qualified corpus contains about 3.03 million quads; this is not evidence for 500 million entities.",
    "Each native trial pins 0, 1, 8, 32 or 300 distinct versions, interleaving one head update between pins. Then it times 300 head replacement transactions over 100 existing Works. Every retained head is checked after all writes.",
    "Raw head replacements measure the TDB mechanism. They omit command admission, SHACL, receipts, outbox and Lucene maintenance. Pin setup writes are outside the timed 300 commits and outside reported file/I/O growth.",
    "Heap and RSS peaks are samples every 10 commits, with final samples, not continuous maxima. Held/released heap is sampled after explicit System.gc requests. File growth is logical length; processWriteBytes is Linux process write accounting.",
    "Copy trials enumerate current/revisions/public-search/control graphs. They stop at a sampled 256 MiB heap-growth cap or 10 seconds, checking every 1000 quads. A partial copy is aborted. Named copies hold the TDB writer; memory copies hold a read transaction.",
    "Copy heap growth includes caches, live objects and garbage. An incomplete bounded copy is not a measurement of full-copy retained memory or an impossibility proof for every optimized copy design.",
    "Trials ran sequentially once on a shared Docker Desktop host. No causal latency regression or improvement is inferred from the differences between trials.",
    "Native phases all passed in the first measured run, whose overall exit was 1 because the copy probe needed an explicit abort on its incomplete memory transaction. That cleanup and separate stdout/stderr capture were fixed; both copy trials then passed. Native measurement code was unchanged by that fix."
  ],
